# Omi Alpha — findings by Qwen 3.8 Flash (self-excluded: unattributed stealth codename, no verified model of that name)

## Exclusion note

**No scores are asserted for `omi-alpha`.** As of 2026-10-23, there is **no identifiable AI model named "Omi Alpha"** from any lab, product, or benchmark aggregator. It carries only a **scaffolded `meta.json`** ("Omi Alpha model evaluation entry / 128K / Text in/out / Standard pricing") with no provider, no repo, and no product page. Every web sweep for "Omi Alpha" as an LLM **collapses onto *other* things**: the documented OpenCode/OpenRouter stealth codename **"ox-alpha"** (a *different* alias, since de-anonymized as Z.ai GLM-5.3-Flash), and the unrelated **BasedHardware "Omi"** AI-wearable / "OMI Obsidian" productivity tool. The `openrouter.ai/stealth/omi-alpha` endpoint returns **404**. There is **no first-party model card, no technical report, no Artificial Analysis / OpenRouter / Vals row, and no independent press** for an LLM called Omi Alpha. Per `RULES.md` (research permanence + no-fabrication + no-reattribution), this is **excluded**, not scored.

### Why this is an exclusion rather than a score

- **No identity anchor.** Unlike a freshly-shipped short-named real model (**Flint** — resolvable to Recursive Intelligence with a launch date, HF repo and press), Omi Alpha resolves to **no maker or product** at all — only a curated guess.
- **Search-collapse is not evidence.** The fact that search engines substitute **"ox-alpha"** does *not* license scoring omi-alpha as ox-alpha: they are **distinct codenames**, and ox-alpha is itself already de-anonymized (GLM-5.3-Flash) with its **own** folder/report. Attributing omi-alpha to ox-alpha (or to any guessed parent) would be **fabrication + reattribution**, which `RULES.md` forbids.
- **Zero capability data.** No benchmark absolute of any kind exists to normalize against; the scaffold's "128K / text" is generic boilerplate applied to many placeholder entries, not a corroborated spec.
- **Stealth-codename pattern.** OpenCode/OpenRouter have run anonymous aliases (ox-alpha, hunter-alpha, MissingNo). A bare "-alpha" slot with no verifiable footprint fits that mold — its true underlying model is **unknown**, so it must not be invented here.

